extraction_notes: "WB30 D-Bees of North America printed 159-161 (cache p160-p162), every number read off 200 dpi renders. The stat block (printed 160) is headed Posluznik R.C.C. - Optional Player Character or NPC; the Wilderness line, secondary skills, equipment and money run onto printed 161. || CATEGORY: Available O.C.C.s: None, so the R.C.C. is the whole class, with its own related and secondary skills; no O.C.C. pairing can be stated as none in occ_restrictions, so it is a restriction line. || XP: the book says use the Body Fixer experience table. Per the class-import reference (a class whose book names another class''s table copies that ladder, Nate''s decision 2026-09-26) the ladder is copied from the production body-fixer row, read 2026-10-03. This departs from the batch brief''s no-xp_table default, which covers races that use their O.C.C.''s table. || POOLS: Hit Points printed P.E. attribute number 1D6 per level, read as P.E. plus 1D6 per level. S.D.C. 2D6+25 stored as sdc_base because the R.C.C. takes no O.C.C., so no occupation pool exists for it to override; men_of_arms is therefore not stated. P.P.E. 2D6. Horror Factor 10 stored as horror_factor (the one it imposes). || PSIONICS: Major Psychic, I.S.P. M.E. x2 plus 1D6 per level. Powers by catalog name: Bio-Regeneration (the Healing power), Deaden Pain, Empathy, Healing Touch, Object Read (Psychometry), Psychic Diagnosis, Psychic Surgery, See Aura, Sense Time, Sixth Sense, Total Recall. || SKILLS: catalog base plus printed bonus: Language: Other 50+20, Literacy: Native Language 40+20, Literacy: Other 30+20, Anthropology 20+10, Biology 30+30, Brewing 25+10, Chemistry 30+15, Field Surgery 16+25 (4%/level), Forensics 35+10, Holistic Medicine 20+10, Medical Doctor 60+15, Sewing 40+20, Xenology 30+20; Law and Mathematics: Basic at catalog base. W.P. Knife/Scalpel is W.P. Knife. MORTUARY SCIENCE has no catalog row; the book prints base 25% +5% per level and the list gives +25%, so it is a special ability at 50%, +5% per level. || HAND TO HAND: none granted; Basic costs one related pick and Expert two, nothing else offered: hand_to_hand costs { basic: 1, expert: 2 }. || RELATED: four, plus one at 4, 8 and 12. Physical excludes Acrobatics, Gymnastics, Boxing and Juicer skills; the catalog''s Juicer-only Physical rows are Juicer Football and Murderthon. Pilot: Automobile, Truck or Hover Vehicle (ground), the last as Hover Craft (ground). Wilderness: Identify Plants and Fruits as Identify Plants & Fruit. SECONDARY: four, plus one at 4, 8 and 15. || BONUSES: +2 roll with impact stored. +3 save vs Horror Factor involving blood and gore is conditional and is ability text. || EQUIPMENT: catalog rows: clothing x2 (work clothing), dress-clothing x2 (fine suits), goggles or sunglasses, medical-kit, scalpel (the collection of scalpels), optics-band, backpack, palm-bio-unit, disposable-surgical-gloves (100 pairs), flashlight, gas-mask, pocket-computer (palm computer), knife x1D4+2 (1D6 to 1D8 S.D.C. each), vibro-knife, laser-scalpel, and an energy pistol of choice from catalog pistols. NOT STORED, no catalog row: sturdy boots, medical scrubs, notebooks, pens and pencils, hand sanitizer, two duffel bags, jars for embalmed parts, multi-tool, books and data libraries; they are in GM Notes. || MONEY: 3D6x1,000 credits. || NOT STORED: size 6 ft 2 in to 8 ft, weight 120-180 lbs, life span 2D6+90 years, NPC experience level 1D8+2, pronunciation, Also known as (Undertakers, Puz Surgeons), habitat, slave market value 6D6x10,000, allies and enemies."
