## Lore

The Posluznik are tall, pale, solemn humanoids from another dimension,
only lately arrived on Rifts Earth. They stand around seven feet, with
long limbs, deft long-fingered hands, large kindly eyes and blue-black
hair, and both sexes favour sturdy black work clothes and formal suits.
Their skin is a patchwork of scars and stitches, partly from practising
surgery on themselves and partly ritual, and they wear it with pride.

Their name is a title meaning one who serves, and they live by a code of
helpfulness, duty and quiet professionalism. A town with a Posluznik in
residence can shrug off maiming and deadly injury, because the D-Bee
carries body parts kept alive in secret embalming fluids, ready to graft
onto a patient. They are often first on the scene of an accident or a
fight, tending the living and harvesting the dead.

When one of them dies, the family gathers to receive his usable limbs and
organs in a custom called Nasljedstvo, and the rest is cremated. Across
the Megaverse they work as surgeons, morticians, medical examiners,
forensic investigators and counsellors, and some of the most respected
cosmetic and reconstructive surgeons anywhere are Posluznik.

## GM Notes

The book heads the race an optional player character or NPC.

Also carried, with no catalog row: sturdy boots, medical scrubs,
notebooks, pens and pencils, hand sanitizer, two duffel bags, jars for
embalmed parts, a multi-tool, books on anatomy, science and local laws,
and data libraries of medical texts. They favour light armor if any, and
prefer magic or force fields.

Size 6 feet 2 inches to 8 feet (1.9 to 2.4 m). Weight 120 to 180 pounds
(54 to 81 kg). Life span 2D6+90 years, though parts of them live on for
generations. NPC experience level 1D8+2. Pronounced pose-LOOZH-nik; also
called Undertakers and Puz Surgeons.

Habitat: anywhere their services are needed, CS ''Burbs and battle fronts
included. Slave market value 6D6x10,000; prized as family doctors.

Allies: welcome in nearly every circle. Enemies: slavers, the Splugorth,
Gene-Splicers, Necromancers and religions that call them abominations.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'posluznik');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'posluznik';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-posluznik-class.sql');
